  "id": "Compound::DB00304 - Gene::6462",
  "verbalization": "Desogestrel, a progestin, is linked to Shbg through multiple pathways that converge on the shared mechanism of progestin action. The evidence suggests that Desogestrel, as part of the Progesterone Congeners class, binds to Shbg through its progestin-like properties. This is supported by the fact that both Desogestrel and Norethindrone, which are also progestin derivatives, bind to Shbg, with their lowest common ancestors pointing to progestin and 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid. Similarly, Etonogestrel, which is structurally similar to Desogestrel, binds to Shbg, reinforcing the role of progestin in this interaction. The recurring theme of progestin and steroid binding suggests a general mechanism by which progestin compounds interact with Shbg, potentially through shared receptor binding sites or molecular recognition patterns. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of progestin in mediating the interaction between Desogestrel and Shbg, with the underlying mechanism likely involving the progestin receptor or a related molecular pathway.",
